Z||000007||Seanh||10-23-2000||11:49 AM||||I think the one about the Momo steering wheels was the one that promoped this. I agree whole heatedly with you guys on this. Unless your actually selling somthing you have in hand and ready to be shipped, then it shouldnt be posted in the mall IMO. Now if some one, who had 1000's of cheap momo steering wheels came in some where other then the mall and started posting all these pictures of his steering wheels and all kinds  of ads, that would probally be spamming. I think a certian individual (it will be obvious from reading the steering wheel thread) was just angry, or woke up on the wrong side of bed that morning and got mad some one told of where they got their steering wheel and offered to give his information out so that others looking for a new wheel could get one at a good price.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tigger||10-23-2000||12:19 PM||||I'm not sure if there's that much of a problem with people spamming here on the board.  I've been concerned about the spam I get in my email.<P>Ever since I joined the forum.  I've been getting spammed for "Low interest Loans," "Penny Stocks," and worse "Free Teen Sex" spams.  I've had two accounts with seperate email addresses, and as soon as I signed up here with each one I immediately have been getting spammed.  I keep blocking the a$$#@l&s, but they keep sending me spam from different addresses.<P>Anyone else getting the same e-mail spams?<P>A little advertisement or "Hey guys, check these out..." for products doesn't bother me as much as these spams.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000009||fiero56||10-23-2000||12:38 PM||||I noticed the same thing when I signed up here. My hotmail accout had never received a single picece of SPAM. But the day I signed up here with my hotmail account, I started receiving almost a dozen SPAMs a day, and it hasn't stopped.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||10-23-2000||12:41 PM||||I get 3-4 Spams a day. Not a big deal. I just delete 'em. If I felt that strongly, I'd just filter 'em. <BR>I'm with you guys. I have no problem with folks passing along info about stuff they find for sale, in *whatever* forum they deem appropriate. Jeez, it's just a freaking post. If you're not interested, then don't read it. When you post a flame, you're only consuming more server space. (Much as I am, here.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000011||william_thorniii||10-23-2000||12:55 PM||||Tigger, 56 & Raydar,<P>That is odd that you mentioned that you have started getting spam since you signed up for this forum.  I get perhaps one piece per day, but has almost always come from another site (i.e. carparts.com.... I wish I would have remembered to check that box).  I have never gotten anything racy, maybe Tigger will need to send me those links j/k.  :~p<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
